  "notes": "San Francisco’s laid-back luxury rap — Bay tempo with none of the hyphy energy. The parameter that separates him from the other sample-warm entries here is **continuity**: no rolls and no fills at all, so the loop reads as unbroken. Minimal, dry kit with very little layering, and a walking sampled bass under the sample’s own changes. ⚠ `medium`: tempo and key measured; the drum specifics are partly lane-inferred and marked `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
